u are actually deficient (which is rare). High doses can also skew medical lab tests like thyroid and hormone panels.\n- **Zinc:** Supports tissue maintenance and normal hair follicle function.[[1]](https://health.clevelandclinic.org/the-best-vitamins-supplements-and-products-for-healthier-hair)[[2]](https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/news/topic/do-hair-growth-vitamins-actually-work/)[[3]](https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/best-vitamins-hair-growth)[[4]](https://www.ulta.com/discover/beauty-education/best-vitamins-for-hair-growth)[[5]](https://www.gnc.com/buy/vitamins-for-hair-loss)\n\n### Popular Hair Growth Supplements\n\n- **Nutrafol:** A multi-ingredient formula targeting stress response, inflammation, and DHT (a hormone linked to hair loss) with ingredients like ashwagandha and saw palmetto.\n- **Viviscal:** A supplement featuring a marine collagen and protein complex combined with biotin, zinc, and iron.[[1]](https://www.ulta.com/discover/beauty-education/best-vitamins-for-hair-growth)\n\n### Important Safety Tips\n\n- **Bloodwork First:** Ask a doctor for a blood test to check your iron, ferritin, and vitamin D levels before starting specific high-dose supplements.\n- **Watch Out for Excess:** Taking too much of certain nutrients\u2014like vitamin A or selenium\u2014can actually cause your hair to fall out.\n- **Lab Interference:** Always tell your doctor if you take biotin before getting blood tests.[[1]](https://www.conwaymedicalcenter.com/news/topic/do-hair-growth-vitamins-actually-work/)[[2]](https://www.hairclub.com/blog/best-vitamins-for-hair-growth/)[[3]](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lUmgXJ1cQNk&t=20)\n\nIf you'd like to narrow this down, tell me:\n\n- Are you dealing with **gradual thinning** or **sudden shedding**?\n- Have you had any **recent blood tests** showing low levels?", "items": [{"type": "ai_overview_element", "position": "left", "title": null, "text": "Vitamins and minerals support hair growth best when you have an actual nutrient d